<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thomas Bowdich</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">visited Kumasi <a href="/years/1817">1817</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thomas Bowdich was an English traveller and writer who visited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumasi">Kumasi</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Ashanti</a> capital, as a British envoy in 1817. His published account is a major early European source on the Ashanti Empire. He described wide paved roads, buildings decorated with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adinkra">Adinkra symbols</a>, a disciplined standing army and elaborate court ceremonies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thomas-bowdich.jpg" alt="Thomas Bowdich" width="320" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: William Derby · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thomas_Edward_Bowdich.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Kumasi's sophistication impressed European visitors: the British envoy <b>Thomas Bowdich</b>, who visited in 1817, described broad, clean streets, houses ornamented with elaborate relief decoration, disciplined troops and court ceremonies of remarkable splendour.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ashanti-empire">Ashanti Empire · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>Much of the evidence comes from European visitors, among them <b>Thomas Bowdich</b>, who reached Kumasi in 1817, and from Asante traditions.</blockquote><a href="/societies/ashanti">Social Hierarchy of the Ashanti Empire</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bristol">Bristol</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-kingdom">the United Kingdom</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banjul">Banjul</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=51.45,-2.6&amp;year=1817" aria-label="Bristol on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4491 382 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Thomas Bowdich"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4941 652h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4941 652h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=51.45,-2.6&amp;year=1817">What was here in 1817? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
